# [PS12 #1] In the formula se(Bjhat) = sigma-hat / sqrt(SST_j (1 - R_j^2)), what is X_j?
#   - The dependent variable Y.
#   - The residuals from the regression.
#   - The independent variable whose coefficient Bjhat we want the standard error of.
#   - Whichever independent variable has the largest coefficient.
#   ANSWER: The independent variable whose coefficient Bjhat we want the standard error of.

# [PS12 #2] In wage = B0 + B1 educ + B2 exper + B3 tenure + U, you want se(B2hat), the standard error of the exper coefficient. Which regression gives R_j^2?
